# ============================================================================
# FILE: .gitignore
# PURPOSE: Tells Git which files and folders to completely ignore and 
#          never upload to GitHub or Cloudflare.
# ============================================================================

# IGNORE BUILD OUTPUT: 
# When Astro builds your website, it generates final web pages in a 'dist' folder. 
# We ignore this because Cloudflare generates its own fresh build automatically.
dist/

# IGNORE GENERATED TYPES: 
# Astro automatically creates a hidden folder called '.astro' to keep track 
# of code definitions on your computer. It shouldn't be shared online.
.astro/

# IGNORE DEPENDENCIES: 
# The 'node_modules' folder holds all the third-party libraries (like XLSX, Astro, etc.). 
# It is usually gigabytes in size and gets downloaded fresh, so we never push it.
node_modules/

# IGNORE LOG FILES: 
# These are temporary diagnostic logs generated by npm, yarn, or pnpm if something goes wrong.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# IGNORE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES: 
# Your '.env' files hold secret keys, passwords, or database credentials. 
# Ignoring them keeps your private keys safe and prevents them from leaking on GitHub.
.env
.env.production

# IGNORE MAC-SPECIFIC FILES: 
# Mac computers automatically hide a '.DS_Store' file inside folders to remember 
# window layouts. Windows users don't need it, so we ignore it.
.DS_Store

# IGNORE JETBRAINS SETTINGS: 
# If you or an editor use JetBrains tools, this ignores their personal workspace settings folder.
.idea/

# IGNORE TEMPORARY MICROSOFT EXCEL LOCK FILES: 
# When you have an Excel spreadsheet open, Microsoft Excel creates temporary 
# hidden system files starting with '~' or '~$'. This rule forces Git to 
# completely ignore them so they never accidentally get pushed to GitHub or Cloudflare!
~*
~$*